          <p class="cm-repat"><span class="cm-repat-year">1959–84</span> Chongryon organized a mass repatriation campaign that sent <b>≈90,000 people</b> to North Korea — most of whom found conditions far worse than promised and were unable to leave.</p>

          <p class="cm-field-caption"><em>The division was not of the community's making.</em> The single gold mark holds the seam — the many who wanted only to keep living where they already lived.</p>
